Derived from kickmix. The simulation semantics (operation set, condition stack,
128-bit fixed-precision angles, global phase, HMR/R measurement outcomes,
operation-statistics counting including INFO_TAG and PUSH/POP_CONDITION), the
random-number chain (std::seed_seq -> mt19937_64 -> ChaCha8 keys, per-256-shot
seeding) and the .kmb file layout follow kickmix (distributed in Google's
Qualtran project, https://github.com/quantumlib/Qualtran, directory kickmix/),
Copyright Google LLC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. This crate
is an independent Rust re-implementation checked for per-shot equality against
kickmix. Where semantics were taken from kickmix source (sim/sim.h,
util/chacha.h, util/fixed_precision_angle_128.*, circuit .kmb reader,
py/interactive_simulator.pybind.cc, py/operation_statistics.pybind.cc), the
attribution above applies.

Official verifier logic. The task adapters (python/kickmix_engine/dqi.py,
invsqrt.py) load the competition's official verifier modules at run time and
call their functions; the verifiers are not included in this repository. The
DQI sampler (src/dqi_sample.rs) re-implements the behaviour of the official
`sample_shots`, and tests/test_engine.py restates that function for testing.
The official verifiers are Copyright Google LLC, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

NumPy algorithms. src/dqi_sample.rs re-implements, to reproduce NumPy's output
exactly, the algorithms of NumPy's PCG64 bit generator (the PCG XSL-RR 128/64
generator by Melissa O'Neill, with NumPy's 32-bit buffering), its 53-bit double
conversion, its bounded-integer method (Lemire) and its Generator.choice
algorithms. NumPy is Copyright NumPy Developers, BSD-3-Clause licence. No NumPy
source code is included.

Test data. tests/data/random_ops.kmb and random_ops_ref.npz were generated with
kickmix by tests/make_fixtures.py. tests/data/dqi_logged_failing_shots.jsonl
records failing shots observed by the owner when running the official DQI
verifier on two public, Apache-2.0 competition circuits.

